# Teamwork announced, then made unpayable while the cast is paid for (CR 601.2g-h, 733.1). Bot1's two Llanowar Elves have
# total power 2, so We Say Thee Nay! may be cast with teamwork. Mana abilities are activated before the costs are paid
# (CR 601.2g): tapping one Elf for {G} towards the {1} leaves one untapped Elf of power 1, so teamwork's "tap creatures
# with total power 2" cannot be paid. Unpayable costs can't be paid (CR 601.2h) and the cast is illegal: it is reversed
# (CR 733.1) without asking which creatures to tap, a question that would have no answer. The spell is back in hand, the
# Elf untapped, and the {U} floating from before the cast still in the pool. Bot1 casts it again without teamwork, paying
# with that {U} and an Elf; Bot2 pays the ransom of {2} from Black Lotus, and the Bolt resolves.

